<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1 Results reviewed by AC &amp; BOD in meetings held on 09.08.2023. SA conducted ltd. review of UFR.   2 UFR prepared in acc. with Ind-AS, u/s 133 of Co. Act read with Cos. (IAS) Rules, 2015.   3 Fig. for Q4 rep. derived fig. b/w audited fig. in respect of full rel. FY &amp; unaudited published yr. to date fig. upto 31st Dec., date of end of Q3 of rel. FY.   4 Rly. Bd. vide CC no. CC60 of 2019 inc. catering tariff for post &amp; pre-paid trains. However, effect of inc. of LF from 18.11.19 to 22.03.20 (for post paid trains) &amp; 27.11.21 to 30.06.23 (for post &amp; pre-paid trains) on a/c of inc. in tariff, has not been recognized. After resumption of regular train services, Co. started sales assessment in 22-23. Further, Co. raised demand notices for inc. LF for pre-paid trains, but some of licensees challenged in Hon’ble HC of Mumbai. As the matter is sub-judice, impact of inc. in LF for pre-paid &amp; post paid trains has not been recognized in fin. for Q3 &amp; for previous years up to 31.03.23.   5 Co. has recognized Rly Share of Rs.182.03 Lakhs @ 15% of profit of RN for Q3 &amp; for pre. FY 2022-23 of Rs.546.60 lakhs. During 21-22, Rs.2713.32 lakhs was paid &amp; charged to revenue on a/c of 15% Rly share in profits of RN plants up to 31.03.21 as Rlys have not agreed. No provision was made for FY 21-22 in view of loss incurred in RN after considering payment of Rs.2713.32 lakhs as expense for that year.    6 In respect of 4 PPP RN plants, DCOs are to be reimbursed GST (net of ITC) availed by them. Impact of Rs.442.46  Lakhs ( FY 21-22 Rs. 309.28 Lakhs) was for 02 plants. DCOs represented against claim of Co. Matter is being examined.   7 NAA issued notice dated 25.02.22 for profiteering amt. of Rs.5041.44 Lakhs u/s 171 of CGST Act. SCN has been contested &amp; matter was argued in Aug.’22 but final is still awaited. Now proceedings, if any, will be commenced afresh by CCI &amp; no communication has been received from CCI.   8 Arbitration award was pronounced in Apr’22 of Rs.7400 Lakhs &amp; simple int. @6% pa from July’18 onwards, in favour of certain licensees. Co. has filed objections. Next date of hearing is 09.10.23.   9 (a) Co. has received revised fixed, variable &amp; Custody charges for 02 Tejas trains w.e.f 13.08.21. Provision made for Q3 at revised rates. However, provision for PY (13.08.21 to 31.03.23) for Rs.5190.40 Lakhs &amp; shown as an excep. items in the FR for Q3 even though the Co. has made representation. (b) For PY, net Y on a/c of Excep. items of Rs.2720.00 Lakhs includes: (i) Rs.1198.59 Lakhs excess provisions written back for PY for PRP, (ii) Rs. 1085.74 lakhs excess provisions written back for PY for Maintenance &amp; Development charges for IT &amp; (iii) Rs. 435.67 Lakhs excess provisions written back for PY for various other expenses.   10 MoR in its ltr. dated 23.2.2023 stated that non-availability of catering services in trains even after 03 days from the date of intimation by Zonal Rlys, shall attract a fine of Rs. 01 lakh per day till the services commence. Co. represented to MoR. Response from MoR is awaited. Amt. of fine till 30.06.23 is neither ascertained nor any demand from Zonal Rlys received till date.   11 Arbitral Tribunal award, earlier kept in reserve, in C&amp;K vs IRCTC case was sent in original to ICA, involving Claim of C&amp;K against Co. of Rs. 2270 Lakhs along with interest, for its pronouncement &amp; release in accordance with rule 68(a) of Domestic Commercial Arbitration 2022 &amp; intimation of the same was given to the Co. on 03.08.23. As per said Rule, when an award has been made, Registrar shall furnish a true copy of award to parties by registered post provided the arbitration costs have been fully paid to Council. Co. has deposited its share of arbitration cost on 07.08.23 whereas the payment status of C&amp;K is not known. In the absence of copy of award, the impact for the same on FR for Q3 is not known.   12. The fig. for the previous year/periods have been regrouped/reclassified/restated, wherever considered necessary.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
